From 5e0718beb1a550cda19b684a9dd942ba488eccbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:43:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0132: fix the HUD numbers with a full parent-chain walk
 (log-41)

Log-41 confirms H3: the (263,71) layout is in neither TxtCounter's local (0,0) nor its parent Capture03's local (0,-100) -- the full chain (TxtCounter -> Capture03 -> RootPane) sums to (0,-100), not (263,71), so the layout is not in the +0x30 chain at all. 0130 had zero effect because its fallback only ran when the pane's own local was non-zero and only read the immediate parent.

The stored original is now rebuilt from the FULL parent chain (the sum of the local translations (+0x30) from the pane up to the root, never any +0x70), when the pane has a matched parent (the unparent subtraction is spurious for a static child that never inherited its parent's move) or when its live matrix was never composed. The 'same transform' early return now only applies when the original came from that chain-walk, killing the spurious early return log-41 confirms (PicIconSh e_orig 88 = g -52 minus pm -140, TxtTotalShine e_orig 195 = 55 minus -140).

Honest result: the regional panes are rebuilt correctly ((-52,10), (55,0)) and move; the coins numbers still land off-screen in x (-140) with this fix alone, because their (263,71) layout is not in the chain -- a further probe must find where it lives. Host: hud_edge_0130_test 32/32, hud_probe_test 57/57, hud_edge_0132_test 32/32 (new, log-41 state); ARM clean (0 udf, 0 umin, no ADDI >= 4096); edge 818 -> 805 words, BINDING v11.
